{"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage"]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"FirebladeECS"}],"role":"article","title":"Choosing a storage"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the sparse-set or the archetype storage for a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and know what changes."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Benchmarks","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keeps its entities and components in one of two storages, chosen when it is created:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let nexus = Nexus()                       \/\/ the default, same as Nexus(storage: .archetype)","let churning = Nexus(storage: .sparseSet) \/\/ for heavy add\/remove churn"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both storages offer the same API with the same observable behavior: generational entity identifiers, events, the structural lock and its traps, families, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading:writing:)"},{"type":"text","text":", spans, snapshots, cloning and the entity state machine. Every test of the package runs against both. What differs is where the components live in memory, and with it what is cheap."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/default","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Nexus()"},{"type":"text","text":" uses it. Choose "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" explicitly for workloads dominated by heavy component add and remove churn (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#Which-storage-to-pick","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). There is no storage protocol: the set of storages is closed, and a nexus switches on its storage once per call, so each storage compiles to concrete code."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"The-sparse-set-storage","text":"The sparse-set storage"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keeps one dense array per component type, a paged sparse index per type that maps an entity to its slot in that array, and a bitset of component types per entity. Adding or removing a component touches the data of that one type only, and no other component moves. Looking up one component is a sparse index read plus an array read."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating a family is the weak spot: the members of a family are stored in each component array in the order the components were added, so every extra component type costs a lookup per member, and the reads are scattered once the arrays were shuffled by churn."}]},{"text":"The archetype storage","level":3,"anchor":"The-archetype-storage","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" follows the design of "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": entities with exactly the same component types live in one table, with a column (an array) per component type. An index maps every entity to its table and row. Tables are created when a component set appears first, and adding or removing one component type moves the entity’s row to another table along a cached edge of the table graph."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating a family visits the tables that match it, and walks their columns linearly: no lookup per member and a sequential read per component. The list of matching tables is cached per family, which the nexus lists when the family is created and extends when a new table appears. A table that became empty stays alive, along with its columns and its entry in the cached lists, where an iteration skips it. Cleaning the nexus with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/clear()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" drops all tables."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In flecs this is the default, and sparse components are the opt-in trait ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sparse"},{"type":"text","text":"): “Sparse components are stored outside of tables, which means they do not have to be moved”, trading query speed for component add and remove speed (see "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/SanderMertens\/flecs\/blob\/master\/docs\/ComponentTraits.md","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). Fireblade 1.x was the reverse, a sparse set per component type; the two storages make that a choice per nexus instead of per component."}]},{"text":"What the numbers say","level":3,"anchor":"What-the-numbers-say","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Measured with 10 000 entities, release build, Apple silicon, wall clock p50 per pass ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"make benchmark"},{"type":"text","text":", see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Benchmarks\/"},{"type":"text","text":"):"}]},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Case"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sparse set"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Archetype"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"11 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2.5 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, B)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"18 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4.3 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, B, C, D)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"31 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"7.7 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, writing: B)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"17 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4.4 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, B, writing: C)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"23 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"6.1 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 reads, 10% of the entities match"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"3.6 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1.3 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 reads, 100 000 entities with shuffled storage order"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"227 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"27 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 reads, 1 024 different component sets"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"18 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"11 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Parameter pack, 5 reads and 2 writes"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 200 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1 800 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"type":"text","text":" over a family, 2 components"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"455 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"455 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Random "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"entity.get"},{"type":"text","text":" of one component, 10 000 lookups"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"334 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"345 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add a component to each entity and remove it again, 10 000 entities"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 180 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4 900 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create and destroy 1 000 entities with 7 components"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1 730 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 510 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row","type":"table","alignments":["left","right","right"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Fireblade 1.x needed 480 μs for the plain iteration of one component and 1 220 μs for two ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IterOnlyOneComponent"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IterOnlyTwoComponents"},{"type":"text","text":"). Both storages iterate without any allocation."}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Iterating with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading:writing:)"},{"text":" is 1.6 to 8 times faster on the archetype storage: about 4 times in the plain case, 8 times when the sparse-set arrays are shuffled against each other, and least when the entities are spread over many small tables.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Changing the component set of an entity costs about twice as much on the archetype storage: the whole row moves. An entity that changes its component set less than once in a few frames is far ahead on iteration; a world that toggles a component on most entities every frame is better off with the sparse set.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Plain ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"text":" iteration and random access cost the same on both: they look every component up per entity.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Entity creation and destruction are a bit slower on the archetype storage, because the row of every component moves with the entity.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"text":"Which storage to pick","level":3,"anchor":"Which-storage-to-pick","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default is the archetype storage: it iterates faster (see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), and iteration is what most worlds spend their time on."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The trade-off: the archetype storage buys iteration speed with the cost of moving a row whenever the component set of an entity changes. Prefer "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" when the workload is dominated by heavy add and remove churn, for example toggling a component on most entities every frame. This matches flecs, where sparse components are the opt-in trait for components that are added and removed often."}]},{"text":"Differences you can observe","level":3,"anchor":"Differences-you-can-observe","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Iteration order.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The sparse-set storage visits the members of a family in the order of the family’s member list, the archetype storage table by table and row by row, and rows move when entities change tables. Neither order is a contract; use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Entity\/identifier"},{"text":" or your own key if you need one.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Single-type spans.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(reading:_:)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(writing:_:)"},{"text":" view one contiguous array. On the archetype storage a type is stored in one column per table, so if entities with different component sets have the type, the span views a temporary copy made table by table (and the writing variant stores it back when the closure returns, also when it throws). That costs one allocation and a copy per call, and nothing can observe the difference while the closure runs, because the type is locked.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Family spans.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Family\/forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)"},{"text":" passes one batch per matching table on the archetype storage, however the nexus was used before; the sparse-set storage passes shorter batches after churn. Both visit every member exactly once, and the closure must be correct for any batch size.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the spans."}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS"]]},"references":{"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEvent":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A marker protocol for all Nexus events."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexusevent","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NexusEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"NexusEvent","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NexusEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Nexus"}],"title":"Nexus","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Nexus"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ComponentMacro":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Implement registration, cloning, snapshots and inspection for a component from its stored properties."}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro","type":"topic","title":"Generating components with the component macro","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/componentmacro"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/componentSpan(writing:_:)":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Gives ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"text":" write access to all components of a type as one contiguous ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MutableSpan"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(writing:_:)","type":"topic","title":"componentSpan(writing:_:)","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/componentspan(writing:_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"componentSpan","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"genericParameter"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Result"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"writing"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":".Type, ("},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MutableSpan","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s11MutableSpanV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Result","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"rethrows","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Result","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/MigratingToFirebladeECS2":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Move a project from FirebladeECS 1.x to 2.0: components become value types, and every write goes through the nexus."}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","type":"topic","title":"Migrating to FirebladeECS 2","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/migratingtofirebladeecs2"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/init(storage:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Initializes a new Nexus."}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/init(storage:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"storage"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC","text":"Nexus"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"text":"StorageKind","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC11StorageKindO"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/init(storage:)","kind":"symbol","title":"init(storage:)"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEventDelegate":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","abstract":[{"text":"A delegate for receiving Nexus events and errors.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexuseventdelegate","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NexusEventDelegate","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"NexusEventDelegate","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NexusEventDelegate","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ReadingAndWritingComponents":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Read a copy, replace a component or change it in place."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/readingandwritingcomponents","kind":"article","title":"Reading and writing components","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say":{"kind":"section","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage#What-the-numbers-say","abstract":[],"type":"topic","title":"What the numbers say","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","abstract":[{"text":"Learn the API and key types Fireblade provides to compose your game or app logic.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/gettingstartedwithfirebladeecs","kind":"article","title":"Getting started with Fireblade ECS","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/SavingAndLoadingScenes":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","abstract":[{"text":"Store a whole ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus"},{"text":" on disk and load it again with the same entities, components and entity identifiers.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/savingandloadingscenes","kind":"article","title":"Saving and Loading Scenes","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/StorageKind/sparseSet":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"One dense array per component type, a paged sparse index per type, a bitset per entity.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","type":"topic","title":"Nexus.StorageKind.sparseSet","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/storagekind\/sparseset","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"sparseSet"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ReactingToNexusEvents":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","abstract":[{"text":"Observe structural changes and, on request, changes of component values.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/reactingtonexusevents","kind":"article","title":"Reacting to Nexus events","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/componentSpan(reading:_:)":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Gives ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"text":" read access to all components of a type as one contiguous ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Span"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documenta